hor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate A</text><path d="M328.4,136 L328.4,66 L360.4,66 L360.4,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.4" y1="95" x2="358.4" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="344.4" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate B</text></svg>', 'A trolley carrying a 4.0 cm card passing light gates A and B.'),
('dd34565f-e86e-564b-acb2-9c859cfbc7ff', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 23, 23, 'A double-interrupt card has two 2.0 cm segments. A single light gate records 0.040 s for the first and 0.025 s for the second, with 0.30 s between the starts of the two blocks. Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'u = 0.020 ÷ 0.040 = 0.50 m s⁻¹; v = 0.020 ÷ 0.025 = 0.80 m s⁻¹; a = (0.80 − 0.50) ÷ 0.30 = 1.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: speeds. C1: a. A1: a = 1.0 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbb4ccb45-t fgbb4ccb45-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbb4ccb45-t">Double-interrupt card</title><desc id="fgbb4ccb45-d">A trolley carrying a double-interrupt card (two 2.0 cm segments) passing a single light gate.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="400" y2="140" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="140" x2="22" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="70" y1="140" x2="62" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="110" y1="140" x2="102" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="140" x2="142" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="140" x2="182" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="230" y1="140" x2="222" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="270" y1="140" x2="262" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="140" x2="302" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="350" y1="140" x2="342" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="390" y1="140" x2="382" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="40" y="112" width="70" height="22" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="54" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="96" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="68" y="82" width="14" height="30" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="75" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 cm segments</text><line x1="118" y1="123" x2="144.4" y2="123" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,123 142.7,126.4 142.7,119.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><path d="M236,136 L236,66 L268,66 L268,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238" y1="95" x2="266" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="252" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">light gate</text></svg>', 'A trolley carrying a double-interrupt card (two 2.0 cm segments) passing a single light gate.'),
('e7c49284-9c33-530b-966b-6dd0c5b028ad', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 24, 24, 'Why do speeds from a light gate tend to be slightly lower than the instantaneous speed at the gate for an accelerating trolley?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The light gate gives the average speed over the card, which matches the speed at the middle of the card''s time, not when its front reaches the beam', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'For uniform acceleration the average equals the speed at mid-time. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: average over card. C1: mid-time speed. A1: C (The light gate gives the average speed over the card, which matches the speed at the middle of the card''s time, not when its front reaches the beam).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('31a4173a-d343-57fd-a2c3-aa531f063cf4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 25, 25, 'On a 50 Hz ticker tape, the first 5-space section measures 2.0 cm and the next 5-space section 3.5 cm. Calculate the acceleration of the tape.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v₁ = 0.020 ÷ 0.10 = 0.20 m s⁻¹; v₂ = 0.035 ÷ 0.10 = 0.35 m s⁻¹; the mid-points are 0.10 s apart: a = (0.35 − 0.20) ÷ 0.10 = 1.5 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: speeds. C1: time between mid-points. A1: a = 1.5 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 120" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge978b75f-t fge978b75f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge978b75f-t">Two tape sections</title><desc id="fge978b75f-d">A ticker tape with ten spaces; the first five measure 2.0 cm and the next five 3.5 cm.</desc><rect x="24" y="30" width="392" height="32" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="61.1" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="88.1" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="115.2" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="142.2" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="169.3" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="216.6" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="264" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="311.3" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="358.7" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="406" cy="46" r="3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="34,80 40.3,77 40.3,83" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="38.9" y1="80" x2="164.4" y2="80" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="169.3,80 162.9,83 162.9,77" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="101.6" y="92" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 cm</text><line x1="34" y1="64" x2="34" y2="84" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><line x1="169.3" y1="64" x2="169.3" y2="84" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/></svg>', 'A ticker tape with ten spaces; the first five measure 2.0 cm and the next five 3.5 cm.'),
('01e495f2-357f-5097-9342-7fd5c0359b2f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 26, 26, 'A motion sensor records a trolley at 0.40 m at t = 0 and 0.85 m at t = 0.50 s. Calculate its average velocity.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.9', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = (0.85 − 0.40) ÷ 0.50 = 0.90 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δs. C1: ÷ Δt. A1: v = 0.90 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4d8d25a0-bdaa-585c-9cd0-80af0506cf93', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 27, 27, 'A student finds that the ticker-timer frequency is really 48 Hz, not 50 Hz. How does this affect her calculated speeds?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Her speeds are too high, because each interval is really longer than 0.020 s', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = d/t with t underestimated gives v too large. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: true interval longer. C1: v overestimated. A1: A (Her speeds are too high, because each interval is really longer than 0.020 s).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('b2f55ba9-074c-5ac9-be8f-9728eb7b9167', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 28, 28, 'In a video at 30 frames per second, a cyclist moves 0.42 m between frames 10 and 11 and 0.48 m between frames 20 and 21. Calculate her average acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v₁ = 0.42 × 30 = 12.6 m s⁻¹; v₂ = 0.48 × 30 = 14.4 m s⁻¹; Δt = 10 ÷ 30 = 0.333 s; a = (14.4 − 12.6) ÷ 0.3333 = 5.4 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: speeds. C1: time between. A1: a = 5.4 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('92ecd09d-5d8d-568b-ba6e-175f72d37c9c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 29, 29, 'Two light gates 0.80 m apart are passed in 0.50 s by a trolley whose speed at the first gate is 1.2 m s⁻¹. Assuming uniform acceleration, calculate its speed at the second gate.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Average speed = 0.80 ÷ 0.50 = 1.6 m s⁻¹ = (u + v)/2, so v = 2 × 1.6 − 1.2 = 2.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: average speed. C1: (u + v)/2. A1: v = 2.0 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('37e9922a-5880-519d-9c0c-d8e71ce2cb3d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 30, 30, 'A strobe photo of a ball rolling down a slope shows images 2.0 cm, 4.0 cm, 6.0 cm, 8.0 cm apart. What does this show?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Uniform acceleration, because the gaps increase by equal amounts', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Equal increases in distance per interval mean equal increases in speed. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: equal increments. C1: constant a. A1: D (Uniform acceleration, because the gaps increase by equal amounts).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd87d2950-t fgd87d2950-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd87d2950-t">Rolling ball</title><desc id="fgd87d2950-d">Multiflash images of a ball rolling down a slope; successive gaps are 2.0, 4.0, 6.0 and 8.0 cm.</desc><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="390" y2="101" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="40" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="40" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="127.5" y1="101" x2="127.5" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="127.5" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><line x1="215" y1="101" x2="215" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="215" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="302.5" y1="101" x2="302.5" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="302.5" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">15</text><line x1="390" y1="101" x2="390" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="390" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><text x="215" y="139" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">distance / cm</text><circle cx="40" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="75" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="145" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="250" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="390" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Multiflash images of a ball rolling down a slope; successive gaps are 2.0, 4.0, 6.0 and 8.0 cm.'),
('55d29c74-7854-5245-8494-5eb0edfae47d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 31, 31, 'In the strobe photo with gaps 2.0, 4.0, 6.0 and 8.0 cm at 0.10 s intervals, calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The gap increases by 2.0 cm each interval: a = Δs ÷ T² = 0.020 ÷ 0.10² = 2.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: increment. C1: a = Δs/T². A1: a = 2.0 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4ec699f9-t fg4ec699f9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4ec699f9-t">Rolling ball</title><desc id="fg4ec699f9-d">Multiflash images 0.10 s apart of a ball rolling down a slope; successive gaps are 2.0, 4.0, 6.0 and 8.0 cm.</desc><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="390" y2="101" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="40" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="40" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="127.5" y1="101" x2="127.5" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="127.5" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><line x1="215" y1="101" x2="215" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="215" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="302.5" y1="101" x2="302.5" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="302.5" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">15</text><line x1="390" y1="101" x2="390" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="390" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><text x="215" y="139" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">distance / cm</text><circle cx="40" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="75" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="145" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="250" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="390" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Multiflash images 0.10 s apart of a ball rolling down a slope; successive gaps are 2.0, 4.0, 6.0 and 8.0 cm.'),
('c0ade738-0979-50cb-9ddf-cb636360477e', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 32, 32, 'A sound pulse returns to a motion sensor after 6.0 ms, and 0.20 s later a pulse returns after 9.0 ms. Taking sound speed 340 m s⁻¹, calculate the trolley''s average speed between the pulses.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.55', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd₁ = 340 × 6.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 1.02 m; d₂ = 340 × 9.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 1.53 m; v = (1.53 − 1.02) ÷ 0.20 = 2.55 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: first distance. C1: second distance. C1: v. A1: v = 2.55 m s⁻¹.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('38605037-f1a0-530a-b9f3-06d59477ed57', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 33, 33, 'Which source of error is reduced by using a narrower card on a light gate?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The difference between average speed over the card and the speed at the gate', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A shorter card gives a speed closer to the instantaneous value. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: average vs instantaneous. C1: shorter time interval. A1: B (The difference between average speed over the card and the speed at the gate).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9c19dfcc-7b20-5250-bf70-aa1934dd735b', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 34, 34, 'A trolley accelerates uniformly from rest past a light gate 0.45 m down a ramp. The 5.0 cm card takes 0.050 s to pass. Calculate the acceleration (use v² = 2as).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.111', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 0.050 ÷ 0.050 = 1.0 m s⁻¹; a = 1.0² ÷ (2 × 0.45) = 1.11 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v. C1: a = v²/2s. A1: a = 1.11 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1f10503f-917f-55dd-a2a5-5cb776dbd8f8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 35, 35, 'Why might a motion sensor give unreliable readings for a trolley very close to it?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The echo returns before the sensor is ready to detect it (minimum range)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Sensors have a minimum working distance. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: minimum range. C1: echo timing. A1: C (The echo returns before the sensor is ready to detect it (minimum range)).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('47a90a80-ecda-5731-8749-ebea22cd1af4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 36, 36, 'A falling ball is filmed at 50 frames per second. It moves 3.9 cm between two frames and 4.3 cm between the next two. Calculate its acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = Δs ÷ T² = (0.043 − 0.039) ÷ 0.020² = 10 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: T = 0.020 s. C1: a = Δs/T². A1: a = 10 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('703a60fd-0623-5672-954c-8846946af70c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 37, 37, 'A light gate timer reads 0.0625 s for a 2.5 cm card. Calculate the speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 0.025 ÷ 0.0625 = 0.40 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: cm to m. C1: v. A1: v = 0.40 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('7537a8e0-d985-5acc-ba53-79e481c4affc', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 38, 38, 'How could the acceleration of a trolley be measured using only one light gate?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Use a double-interrupt card and measure each block time and the time between them', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Two speeds and the time between them give a. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: two segments. C1: two speeds and interval. A1: A (Use a double-interrupt card and measure each block time and the time between them).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('21ee88b8-74a2-57ae-b9d9-c5e9d15dafe1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 39, 39, 'A ticker tape section of 10 spaces (50 Hz) is 9.0 cm long. Calculate the average speed in this section.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.45', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 10 × 0.020 = 0.20 s; v = 0.090 ÷ 0.20 = 0.45 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: time. C1: v. A1: v = 0.45 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3e97fab0-38e7-50b7-bdeb-cdf5d72657cc', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 40, 40, 'A 4.8 cm card blocks the first light gate for 0.12 s and a second gate 0.80 s later for 0.080 s. Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.25', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'u = 0.048 ÷ 0.12 = 0.40 m s⁻¹; v = 0.048 ÷ 0.080 = 0.60 m s⁻¹; a = (0.60 − 0.40) ÷ 0.80 = 0.25 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: speeds. C1: a. A1: a = 0.25 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('21407022-d4ad-5b51-9640-068f1b61b235', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 41, 41, 'A 25 Hz stroboscope photographs a trolley; successive gaps are 1.6 cm, 2.0 cm and 2.4 cm. Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 1 ÷ 25 = 0.040 s; the gap grows by 0.40 cm: a = 0.0040 ÷ 0.040² = 2.5 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: T and Δs. C1: a = Δs/T². A1: a = 2.5 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg223ca3d9-t fg223ca3d9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg223ca3d9-t">Trolley at 25 Hz</title><desc id="fg223ca3d9-d">Multiflash images of a trolley at 25 Hz; successive gaps are 1.6, 2.0 and 2.4 cm.</desc><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="390" y2="101" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="40" y1="101" x2="40" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="40" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="156.7" y1="101" x2="156.7" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="156.7" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="273.3" y1="101" x2="273.3" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="273.3" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="390" y1="101" x2="390" y2="107" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="390" y="119" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><text x="215" y="139" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">distance / cm</text><circle cx="40" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="133.3" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="250" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="390" cy="75" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Multiflash images of a trolley at 25 Hz; successive gaps are 1.6, 2.0 and 2.4 cm.'),
('f67b3841-a452-5b25-a21e-772b2327d254', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 42, 42, 'A ticker tape from a trolley shows equally spaced dots along its whole length. What is the trolley''s acceleration?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Zero, because equal distances in equal times mean constant velocity', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'No change in the spacing means no change in speed. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: equal spacing. C1: constant velocity. A1: B (Zero, because equal distances in equal times mean constant velocity).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c6684d7e-b98e-53b4-a3a2-ad142a0f8d1a', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 43, 43, 'A light gate gives a speed of 0.40 m s⁻¹ for a 5.0 cm card. The block time has an uncertainty of ±0.002 s. Calculate the percentage uncertainty in the block time.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.6', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 0.050 ÷ 0.40 = 0.125 s; % = 0.002 ÷ 0.125 × 100 = 1.6 %. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: block time. C1: percentage. A1: % uncertainty = 1.6%.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a20567ca-3372-5f2e-a700-ccd3cff2307f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 44, 44, 'A trolley carrying a 3.0 cm card passes gate A (block time 0.060 s) and gate B (block time 0.030 s). Gates A and B are 0.50 m apart. (a) Calculate both speeds. (b) Use v² = u² + 2as to find the acceleration.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.75', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) u = 0.030 ÷ 0.060 = 0.50 m s⁻¹; v = 0.030 ÷ 0.030 = 1.0 m s⁻¹. (b) a = (1.0² − 0.50²) ÷ (2 × 0.50) = 0.75 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: u. C1: v. M1: v² = u² + 2as. C1: value. A1: a = 0.75 m s⁻².', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg79fd40d1-t fg79fd40d1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg79fd40d1-t">Gates 0.50 m apart</title><desc id="fg79fd40d1-d">A trolley carrying a 3.0 cm card passing light gates A and B, 0.50 m apart.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="400" y2="140" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="140" x2="22" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="70" y1="140" x2="62" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="110" y1="140" x2="102" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="140" x2="142" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="140" x2="182" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="230" y1="140" x2="222" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="270" y1="140" x2="262" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="140" x2="302" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="350" y1="140" x2="342" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="390" y1="140" x2="382" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="40" y="112" width="70" height="22" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="54" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="96" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="68" y="82" width="14" height="30" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="75" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.0 cm card</text><line x1="118" y1="123" x2="144.4" y2="123" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,123 142.7,126.4 142.7,119.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><path d="M185.6,136 L185.6,66 L217.6,66 L217.6,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="187.6" y1="95" x2="215.6" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="201.6" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate A</text><path d="M328.4,136 L328.4,66 L360.4,66 L360.4,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.4" y1="95" x2="358.4" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="344.4" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate B</text><polygon points="201.6,162 207.9,159 207.9,165" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="206.5" y1="162" x2="339.5" y2="162" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="344.4,162 338.1,165 338.1,159" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="273" y="174" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.50 m</text></svg>', 'A trolley carrying a 3.0 cm card passing light gates A and B, 0.50 m apart.'),
('4e2800e7-8cc6-558e-9cca-e20b5d78a9d1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 45, 45, 'A strobe flashing at 10 Hz photographs a ball dropped from rest. The images are at 0, 4.9, 19.6, 44.1 and 78.4 cm below the release point. (a) Find the gaps between images. (b) Find the increase in gap per interval. (c) Calculate g.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9.8', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 4.9, 14.7, 24.5, 34.3 cm. (b) 9.8 cm each interval. (c) g = Δs ÷ T² = 0.098 ÷ 0.10² = 9.8 m s⁻². Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: gaps. C1: equal increment. M1: Δs = aT². C1: T = 0.10 s. C1: value. A1: g = 9.8 m s⁻².', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 260 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgcf4b57f9-t fgcf4b57f9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgcf4b57f9-t">Falling ball at 10 Hz</title><desc id="fgcf4b57f9-d">Multiflash images 0.10 s apart of a ball dropped from rest, at 0, 4.9, 19.6, 44.1 and 78.4 cm below the release point.</desc><line x1="104" y1="30" x2="104" y2="300" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="98" y1="30" x2="104" y2="30" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="92" y="30" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="98" y1="97.5" x2="104" y2="97.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="92" y="97.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><line x1="98" y1="165" x2="104" y2="165" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="92" y="165" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><line x1="98" y1="232.5" x2="104" y2="232.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="92" y="232.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">60</text><line x1="98" y1="300" x2="104" y2="300" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="92" y="300" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">80</text><text x="104" y="16" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">cm</text><circle cx="150" cy="30" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="30" x2="141" y2="30" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><circle cx="150" cy="46.5" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="46.5" x2="141" y2="46.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><circle cx="150" cy="96.2" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="96.2" x2="141" y2="96.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><circle cx="150" cy="178.8" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="178.8" x2="141" y2="178.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><circle cx="150" cy="294.6" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="294.6" x2="141" y2="294.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/></svg>', 'Multiflash images 0.10 s apart of a ball dropped from rest, at 0, 4.9, 19.6, 44.1 and 78.4 cm below the release point.'),
('41d6d14f-9e86-528b-b2c5-d25bd36f4e5c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 46, 46, 'A motion sensor gives a trolley''s displacement as 0.20 m at 0.0 s, 0.30 m at 0.5 s and 0.50 m at 1.0 s. (a) Calculate the average velocity in each half-second. (b) Calculate the acceleration, assuming it is uniform.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.10 ÷ 0.5 = 0.20 m s⁻¹; 0.20 ÷ 0.5 = 0.40 m s⁻¹. (b) These are the speeds at 0.25 s and 0.75 s: a = (0.40 − 0.20) ÷ 0.5 = 0.40 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: first velocity. C1: second velocity. M1: mid-interval times. C1: value. A1: a = 0.40 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL),
('1adc0cb5-1909-5d62-8944-71a3690ce3af', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 47, 47, 'A 1.0 cm card is used at a light gate on a trolley accelerating at 2.0 m s⁻². The trolley reaches the gate at 0.40 m s⁻¹. (a) Use s = ut + ½at² to find the block time. (b) Calculate the speed the light gate reports. (c) Calculate the percentage difference from 0.40 m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.902', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Solving 1.0t² + 0.40t − 0.010 (set to zero) gives t ≈ 0.02361 s. (b) v = 0.010 ÷ 0.02361 = 0.4236 m s⁻¹. (c) % = (0.4236 − 0.40) ÷ 0.40 × 100 = 5.90 %. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: quadratic set up. C1: t. C1: reported speed. M1: % difference. C1: value. A1: % difference = 5.90%.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('5ff50b67-efb6-52db-800c-70b673ce5508', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 48, 48, 'A ticker tape (50 Hz) is cut into 5-space strips of lengths 1.0, 1.8, 2.6, 3.4 and 4.2 cm. (a) Explain why the strips can be used as a v–t graph. (b) Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.8', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Each strip is the distance in 0.10 s, proportional to the average speed. (b) Each strip is 0.8 cm longer, so Δv = 0.0080 ÷ 0.10 = 0.080 m s⁻¹ per 0.10 s: a = 0.080 ÷ 0.10 = 0.80 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: strip length ∝ speed. C1: Δv per strip. M1: a = Δv/Δt. C1: value. A1: a = 0.80 m s⁻².', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg65dfe8c0-t fg65dfe8c0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg65dfe8c0-t">Tape-strip chart</title><desc id="fg65dfe8c0-d">Five 5-space strips stuck side by side form a bar chart of strip length: 1.0, 1.8, 2.6, 3.4 and 4.2 cm.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="83.7" y1="34" x2="83.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="143.3" y1="34" x2="143.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="262.7" y1="34" x2="262.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="322.3" y1="34" x2="322.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="200.4" x2="382" y2="200.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="158.8" x2="382" y2="158.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="117.2" x2="382" y2="117.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="75.6" x2="382" y2="75.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="83.7" y1="242" x2="83.7" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-lin