 x1="20" y1="158.8" x2="24" y2="158.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="158.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="117.2" x2="24" y2="117.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="117.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="75.6" x2="24" y2="75.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="75.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="34" x2="24" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">strip number</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">strip length / cm</text><line x1="79.7" y1="196.4" x2="87.7" y2="204.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="79.7" y1="204.4" x2="87.7" y2="196.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="163.1" x2="147.3" y2="171.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="171.1" x2="147.3" y2="163.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="199" y1="129.8" x2="207" y2="137.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="199" y1="137.8" x2="207" y2="129.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258.7" y1="96.6" x2="266.7" y2="104.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258.7" y1="104.6" x2="266.7" y2="96.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="318.3" y1="63.3" x2="326.3" y2="71.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="318.3" y1="71.3" x2="326.3" y2="63.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Five 5-space strips stuck side by side form a bar chart of strip length: 1.0, 1.8, 2.6, 3.4 and 4.2 cm.'),
('a0dc021e-eedb-5afb-838a-daf5daea834c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 49, 49, 'A ball rolls down a ramp and passes two light gates 0.60 m apart. Its speeds are 0.80 m s⁻¹ and 1.4 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the time between the gates, assuming uniform acceleration. (b) Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.1', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) t = 0.60 ÷ ((0.80 + 1.4) ÷ 2) = 0.5455 s. (b) a = (1.4 − 0.80) ÷ 0.5455 = 1.10 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: average speed. C1: time. M1: a = Δv/t. C1: value. A1: a = 1.10 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL),
('3db9ddfd-7ec6-517d-a365-ea3b2640ae97', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 50, 50, 'A camera at 240 frames per second films a sprinter''s start. Her hip moves 1.0 cm between frames 1 and 2 and 2.5 cm between frames 61 and 62. (a) Calculate her speed at each time. (b) Calculate the time between the two measurements. (c) Calculate her average acceleration.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '14.4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.010 × 240 = 2.4 m s⁻¹; 0.025 × 240 = 6.0 m s⁻¹. (b) 60 ÷ 240 = 0.25 s. (c) a = (6.0 − 2.4) ÷ 0.25 = 14.4 m s⁻². Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: first speed. C1: second speed. C1: time. M1: a = Δv/t. C1: value. A1: a = 14.4 m s⁻².', 6, NULL, NULL),
('16762d98-eb5c-5eed-9c10-c094dfa286e7', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 51, 51, 'A student uses a stopwatch to time a trolley over 2.00 m and gets 1.60 s, with a reaction-time uncertainty of ±0.2 s. (a) Calculate the average speed. (b) Calculate the percentage uncertainty in the speed.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12.5', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 2.00 ÷ 1.60 = 1.25 m s⁻¹. (b) % = 0.2 ÷ 1.60 × 100 = 12.5 %. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: speed. M1: % in time. C1: same % in speed. C1: value. A1: % uncertainty = 12.5%.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('12a1b4c0-e729-5d5e-90fb-4c82abe0e597', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 52, 52, 'A falling card 8.0 cm long passes a light gate 0.50 m below its release point. (a) Calculate the speed at the gate from v² = 2gh. (b) Calculate the time the card takes to pass the gate, ignoring the change in speed. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.02554', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = √(2 × 9.81 × 0.50) = 3.132 m s⁻¹. (b) t = 0.080 ÷ 3.132 = 0.0255 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: v² = 2gh. C1: speed. M1: t = L/v. C1: value. A1: t = 0.0255 s.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('147b1efe-f8e9-51f4-92bd-67e639170ec8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '97c777dc-0adf-4df6-bd8f-9c659f0ef783', 'a-level', '2.6', '9702 coursebook 2.6 · Measuring velocity and acceleration', 53, 53, 'A motion sensor records a trolley at 0.50, 0.58, 0.72 and 0.92 m at 0.10 s intervals. (a) Calculate the average velocity in each interval. (b) Calculate the acceleration, assuming it is uniform.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.08 ÷ 0.10 = 0.80, 0.14 ÷ 0.10 = 1.4, 0.20 ÷ 0.10 = 2.0 m s⁻¹. (b) These rise by 0.60 m s⁻¹ every 0.10 s: a = (2.0 − 0.80) ÷ 0.20 = 6.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: velocities. C1: equal increases. M1: Δv/Δt. C1: value. A1: a = 6.0 m s⁻².', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgee5661dd-t fgee5661dd-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgee5661dd-t">Motion-sensor data</title><desc id="fgee5661dd-d">Displacement against time from a motion sensor: 0.50, 0.58, 0.72 and 0.92 m at 0.10 s intervals.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="149.4" y1="34" x2="149.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="265.7" y1="34" x2="265.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="172.7" x2="382" y2="172.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1