><text x="242.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.6</text><line x1="312.2" y1="242" x2="312.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="312.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.8</text><line x1="382" y1="242" x2="382" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="382" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><line x1="29" y1="242" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="29" y1="190" x2="33" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.5</text><line x1="29" y1="138" x2="33" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="138" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><line x1="29" y1="86" x2="33" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5</text><line x1="29" y1="34" x2="33" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0</text><text x="207.5" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">s / m</text><text x="29" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v² / m² s⁻²</text><polyline points="33,242 382,75.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A straight line through the origin on a graph of v² against s, gradient 1.6 m s⁻².'),
('077f49e2-525b-5f24-9e8e-de3e18b92636', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 25, 25, 'A student finds the trolley''s acceleration is much less than g sin θ. What is the most likely cause?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Friction (and rolling resistance) acting up the ramp', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Without friction a = g sin θ. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: friction. C1: opposes motion. A1: D (Friction (and rolling resistance) acting up the ramp).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('77fd33c8-8748-5128-b43c-ed7ae11a0e45', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 26, 26, 'A frictionless trolley on a ramp inclined at 5.0° should have acceleration g sin θ. Calculate it. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.855', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = 9.81 × sin 5.0° = 0.855 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a = g sin θ. C1: value. A1: a = 0.855 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('510077ab-c773-579b-a874-293b58cc3cae', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 27, 27, 'The measured acceleration down a 5.0° ramp is 0.72 m s⁻², while g sin θ is 0.855 m s⁻². Calculate the percentage by which friction reduces the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15.79', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '% = (0.855 − 0.72) ÷ 0.855 × 100 = 15.8 %. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: difference. C1: percentage. A1: % = 15.8%.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('adb9242d-0a01-58ce-a1d5-328dc41e0ed4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 28, 28, 'Why does a v–t graph from light-gate data for a trolley sometimes not pass through the origin even though it started from rest?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The times are measured from when the trolley is released, but the first gate is some distance down the ramp', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Points start part-way along the line; the extrapolated line should pass through the origin. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: first reading after release. C1: extrapolation. A1: B (The times are measured from when the trolley is released, but the first gate is some distance down the ramp).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a7e40393-e12a-5640-be99-3aa2faf58b8f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 29, 29, 'A trolley passes gate A at 0.45 m s⁻¹ and gate B, 0.50 m further on, at 0.85 m s⁻¹. Calculate the time between the gates assuming uniform acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.7692', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 0.50 ÷ ((0.45 + 0.85) ÷ 2) = 0.769 s. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: average speed. C1: t = s/v_avg. A1: t = 0.769 s.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg9e51fece-t fg9e51fece-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg9e51fece-t">Gates 0.50 m apart</title><desc id="fg9e51fece-d">A trolley passing light gates A and B, 0.50 m apart.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="400" y2="140" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="140" x2="22" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="70" y1="140" x2="62" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="110" y1="140" x2="102" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="140" x2="142" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="140" x2="182" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="230" y1="140" x2="222" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="270" y1="140" x2="262" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="140" x2="302" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="350" y1="140" x2="342" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="390" y1="140" x2="382" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="40" y="112" width="70" height="22" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="54" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="96" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="68" y="82" width="14" height="30" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="75" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">card</text><line x1="118" y1="123" x2="144.4" y2="123" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,123 142.7,126.4 142.7,119.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><path d="M185.6,136 L185.6,66 L217.6,66 L217.6,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="187.6" y1="95" x2="215.6" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="201.6" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate A</text><path d="M328.4,136 L328.4,66 L360.4,66 L360.4,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.4" y1="95" x2="358.4" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="344.4" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate B</text><polygon points="201.6,162 207.9,159 207.9,165" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="206.5" y1="162" x2="339.5" y2="162" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="344.4,162 338.1,165 338.1,159" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="273" y="174" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.50 m</text></svg>', 'A trolley passing light gates A and B, 0.50 m apart.'),
('8061a4d9-fb45-597a-8dea-06cf1101834f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 30, 30, 'A trolley released from rest is timed over 0.40 m, 0.80 m and 1.20 m, taking 1.00 s, 1.41 s and 1.73 s. Use the 1.20 m reading to calculate the acceleration, and check it against the 0.40 m reading.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.8019', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = 2 × 1.20 ÷ 1.73² = 0.802 m s⁻². Check: 2 × 0.40 ÷ 1.00² = 0.80 m s⁻², consistent. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: a = 2s/t². C1: value. C1: consistency check. A1: a = 0.802 m s⁻².', 4, NULL, NULL),
('d2da1ce2-5c3c-5a4e-8387-2805dfad7969', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 31, 31, 'Why is the length of the card measured with vernier calipers rather than a metre rule?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The card is short, so a more precise instrument reduces its percentage uncertainty', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A small length needs a small resolution. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: short length. C1: % uncertainty reduced. A1: C (The card is short, so a more precise instrument reduces its percentage uncertainty).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2ad468bc-ea60-5432-a504-ee6de85ff358', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 32, 32, 'The card length is 2.50 ± 0.05 cm and the block time 0.0500 ± 0.0005 s. Calculate the percentage uncertainty in the speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '% = 0.05 ÷ 2.50 × 100 + 0.0005 ÷ 0.0500 × 100 = 3.0 %. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: % in length. C1: % in time, added. A1: % uncertainty = 3.0%.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('28db16b5-5f79-5835-8638-6d950b7647bc', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 33, 33, 'A trolley''s velocity is measured at 0.2 s intervals: 0.10, 0.22, 0.34, 0.46 m s⁻¹. Calculate the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Velocity increases by 0.12 m s⁻¹ every 0.2 s: a = 0.12 ÷ 0.2 = 0.60 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: constant increase. C1: a. A1: a = 0.60 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgafa46b5c-t fgafa46b5c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgafa46b5c-t">Trolley velocities</title><desc id="fgafa46b5c-d">Velocity readings 0.10, 0.22, 0.34 and 0.46 m s⁻¹ at 0.2 s intervals, on a straight line.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="149.4" y1="34" x2="149.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="265.7" y1="34" x2="265.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="200.4" x2="382" y2="200.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="158.8" x2="382" y2="158.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-w