('641c0e4b-4ecc-5b88-a262-958edb26cc1d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 46, 46, 'A trolley on a 6.0° ramp has a measured acceleration of 0.82 m s⁻². (a) Calculate g sin θ. (b) Calculate the deceleration due to friction. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.2054', 'm s⁻²', false, 0.05, false, NULL, '(a) g sin θ = 9.81 × sin 6.0° = 1.03 m s⁻². (b) 1.03 − 0.82 = 0.21 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: g sin θ. C1: value. M1: difference. C1: value. A1: a_f = 0.21 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL),
('d5162f21-1bfd-5b06-96a7-9abced8eec31', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 47, 47, 'Gates A and B are 0.75 m apart. A 5.0 cm card takes 0.10 s at A and 0.050 s at B. (a) Calculate both speeds. (b) Calculate the acceleration. (c) Calculate the time between the gates.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.050 ÷ 0.10 = 0.50 m s⁻¹; 0.050 ÷ 0.050 = 1.0 m s⁻¹. (b) a = (1.0² − 0.50²) ÷ (2 × 0.75) = 0.50 m s⁻². (c) t = (1.0 − 0.50) ÷ 0.50 = 1.0 s. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: u. C1: v. M1: v² = u² + 2as. C1: a. C1: t. A1: t = 1.0 s.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg13b5956c-t fg13b5956c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg13b5956c-t">Gates 0.75 m apart</title><desc id="fg13b5956c-d">A trolley carrying a 5.0 cm card passing light gates A and B, 0.75 m apart.</desc><line x1="20" y1="140" x2="400" y2="140" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="140" x2="22" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="70" y1="140" x2="62" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="110" y1="140" x2="102" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="140" x2="142" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="140" x2="182" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="230" y1="140" x2="222" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="270" y1="140" x2="262" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="140" x2="302" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="350" y1="140" x2="342" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="390" y1="140" x2="382" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="40" y="112" width="70" height="22" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="54" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="96" cy="136" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="68" y="82" width="14" height="30" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="75" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.0 cm card</text><line x1="118" y1="123" x2="144.4" y2="123" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,123 142.7,126.4 142.7,119.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><path d="M185.6,136 L185.6,66 L217.6,66 L217.6,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="187.6" y1="95" x2="215.6" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="201.6" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate A</text><path d="M328.4,136 L328.4,66 L360.4,66 L360.4,136" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.4" y1="95" x2="358.4" y2="95" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="344.4" y="54" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gate B</text><polygon points="201.6,162 207.9,159 207.9,165" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="206.5" y1="162" x2="339.5" y2="162" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="344.4,162 338.1,165 338.1,159" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="273" y="174" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.75 m</text></svg>', 'A trolley carrying a 5.0 cm card passing light gates A and B, 0.75 m apart.'),
('bcf8b773-92c7-5fa4-92fd-c7e2c41f435c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 48, 48, 'A student finds a = 1.55 m s⁻² for a trolley on a 10° ramp, while g sin θ = 1.70 m s⁻². The uncertainty in a is ±0.05 m s⁻². (a) Calculate the range of the measured value. (b) Calculate the percentage difference from g sin θ.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8.824', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1.50 to 1.60 m s⁻². (b) % = (1.70 − 1.55) ÷ 1.70 × 100 = 8.8 %; the difference is beyond the uncertainty, suggesting friction. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: range. M1: % difference. C1: value. B1: conclusion. A1: % difference = 8.8%.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('80264934-8023-5ced-86be-629b05899dd8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 49, 49, 'A trolley''s speed is measured at gates 0.20 m apart: 0.50 m s⁻¹ and then 0.70 m s⁻¹. A third gate 0.20 m further reads 0.86 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate a between the first two gates. (b) Calculate a between the last two gates.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.624', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) (0.70² − 0.50²) ÷ (2 × 0.20) = 0.60 m s⁻². (b) (0.86² − 0.70²) ÷ (2 × 0.20) = 0.624 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: v² = u² + 2as. C1: first a. C1: second a. C1: comparison. A1: a = 0.624 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL),
('061ddd5b-cf19-53ac-9776-f7806bbfbeb3', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 50, 50, 'A ball is released from rest at the top of a 1.80 m ramp and its time to the bottom is 1.20 s. (a) Calculate its acceleration. (b) Calculate its speed at the bottom. (c) A light gate at the bottom gives 2.85 m s⁻¹. Calculate the percentage difference from (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = 2 × 1.80 ÷ 1.20² = 2.5 m s⁻². (b) v = 2.5 × 1.20 = 3.0 m s⁻¹. (c) % = (3.0 − 2.85) ÷ 3.0 × 100 = 5.0 %. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: a. C1: v. M1: % difference. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: % difference = 5.0%.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('de3c98b1-a8b7-583f-a71d-5d95876ce369', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 51, 51, 'A glider of mass 0.40 kg on an air track is accelerated by a resultant force of 0.12 N. Gates 0.60 m apart are passed at 0.50 m s⁻¹ then v. (a) Calculate the acceleration from F = ma. (b) Calculate v.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.781', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = 0.12 ÷ 0.40 = 0.30 m s⁻². (b) v = √(0.50² + 2 × 0.30 × 0.60) = 0.781 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: a. M1: v² = u² + 2as. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: v = 0.781 m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('20b1eaf6-872a-565d-90eb-0d98e55bb3a5', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c16862d4-9430-4015-95fa-20d7cf89a45d', 'a-level', '2.7', '9702 coursebook 2.7 · Determining velocity and acceleration in the laboratory', 52, 52, 'A student measures a trolley''s acceleration on a 6.0° ramp as 0.94 m s⁻². (a) Calculate g sin 6.0°. (b) Calculate the deceleration caused by friction. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.08542', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 9.81 × sin 6.0° = 1.025 m s⁻². (b) 1.025 − 0.94 = 0.085 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: g sin θ. C1: value. M1: difference. C1: value. A1: a_f = 0.085 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL)
