 the area is split into the rectangle ut and the triangle ½at².'),
('dde83122-a9b5-5e12-b004-8d2941ab662c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 9, 9, 'Which equation is obtained by eliminating t between v = u + at and s = (u + v)t/2?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'v² = u² + 2as', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Substitute t = (v − u)/a. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (v² = u² + 2as).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('313ba4f9-8da6-5058-b177-b273d3b1bdf3', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 10, 10, 'Which equation is obtained by substituting v = u + at into s = (u + v)t/2?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 's = ut + ½at²', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(u + u + at)t/2 = ut + ½at². Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (s = ut + ½at²).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('4d524e99-5d2d-529a-8142-a653e5b3b95f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 11, 11, 'Check s = ut + ½at² against s = (u + v)t/2 for u = 2.0 m s⁻¹, a = 4.0 m s⁻² and t = 3.0 s by calculating s.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '24', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = 2.0 × 3.0 + 0.5 × 4.0 × 3.0² = 24 m (and v = 14 m s⁻¹ gives (2.0 + 14) × 3.0 ÷ 2 = 24 m). Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: either route. A1: s = 24 m.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('5a1093ed-6147-5c22-b1b7-76938ff92444', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 12, 12, 'Why must the acceleration be constant for these derivations?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The v–t graph must be a straight line for the area and gradient expressions to hold', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A curved graph has a different area. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (The v–t graph must be a straight line for the area and gradient expressions to hold).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('e191496c-7d24-582e-aee7-e84b9b91e96d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 13, 13, 'Calculate the gradient of a v–t line from u = 3.0 m s⁻¹ to v = 15 m s⁻¹ over t = 4.0 s.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (15 − 3.0) ÷ 4.0 = 3.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: a = 3.0 m s⁻².', 1, NULL, NULL),
('4907ccb2-1758-5756-9be5-0245735e309b', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 14, 14, 'What does the area of the trapezium under a straight v–t line equal?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '½(u + v)t', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Mean of parallel sides times width. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (½(u + v)t).', 1, NULL, NULL),
