('cf29af06-5af4-5b24-b9e7-c319145bd63c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 16, 16, 'Which quantity is absent from s = (u + v)t/2?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The acceleration a', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Useful when a is not known. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (The acceleration a).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('84a0b0fb-a275-5ad5-a18e-20a3c77096d1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 17, 17, 'Using v² = u² + 2as, find v when u = 3.0 m s⁻¹, a = 2.0 m s⁻² and s = 4.0 m.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = √(3.0² + 2 × 2.0 × 4.0) = 5.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: substitution. A1: v = 5.0 m s⁻¹.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('954d1039-2f73-59a7-aea7-a13688e91ffb', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 18, 18, 'Using v = u + at, calculate a when u = 2.0 m s⁻¹, v = 11 m s⁻¹ and t = 3.0 s.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (11 − 2.0) ÷ 3.0 = 3.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: rearranged. A1: a = 3.0 m s⁻².', 2, NULL, NULL),
('936ceab3-23e7-5ca0-9986-e09b8b13bd71', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 19, 19, 'Which equation of motion does not involve the final velocity v?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 's = ut + ½at²', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Use it when v is unknown and not needed. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (s = ut + ½at²).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('488c612c-11dc-52d1-8e14-69dbac1cb79a', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 20, 20, 'Which equation of motion does not involve the displacement s?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'v = u + at', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'It comes straight from the definition of a. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (v = u + at).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('00545cb4-2cc0-5596-8058-c913dbf50efe', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 21, 21, 'Starting from v = u + at, which step gives v² = u² + 2as?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Square to get v² = u² + 2uat + a²t², then use s = ut + ½at² to replace 2a(ut + ½at²) by 2as', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v² = u² + 2a(ut + ½at²) = u² + 2as. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: square. C1: substitute s. A1: D (Square to get v² = u² + 2uat + a²t², then use s = ut + ½at² to replace 2a(ut + ½at²) by 2as).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('91ab5334-9ef6-59bc-ba0d-e86949a71c92', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 22, 22, 'For u = 5.0 m s⁻¹, a = 2.0 m s⁻², t = 4.0 s, calculate v² using v = u + at, and show it equals u² + 2as. Give v² in m² s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '169', 'm² s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 5.0 + 2.0 × 4.0 = 13 m s⁻¹, v² = 169; s = 5.0 × 4.0 + 0.5 × 2.0 × 4.0² = 36 m; u² + 2as = 5.0² + 2 × 2.0 × 36 = 169. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v. C1: check. A1: v² = 169 m² s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('fe8505b9-51ba-56b4-b15d-edba87ff9ed2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 23, 23, 'Derive and use s = vt − ½at² to find s when v = 20 m s⁻¹, a = 3.0 m s⁻² and t = 4.0 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '56', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'With u = v − at in s = (u + v)t/2: s = vt − ½at² = 20 × 4.0 − 0.5 × 3.0 × 4.0² = 56 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: substitute u. C1: value. A1: s = 56 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('51268c79-dafe-59af-8e81-a063e00494d0', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 24, 24, 'Why is s = vt − ½at² useful?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It gives s when the initial velocity is unknown but the final velocity is known', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'It is the "no-u" equation. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: u absent. C1: use. A1: B (It gives s when the initial velocity is unknown but the final velocity is known).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('68ec946e-eb40-5e64-a897-782deaff76df', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 25, 25, 'A car decelerates uniformly to rest in 6.0 s over 45 m. Use s = vt − ½at² with v = 0 to find the deceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'With v = 0, s = −½at², so a = −2 × 45 ÷ 6.0² = −2.5 m s⁻²; the deceleration is 2 × 45 ÷ 6.0² = 2.5 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = 0. C1: value. A1: a = 2.5 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('87188913-f3da-5c81-a1d5-cb3932fa86ad', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 26, 26, 'A v–t graph from u to v in time t is split into a rectangle of height u and a triangle of height (v − u). Which expression for the triangle area leads to ½at²?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '½t(v − u) with v − u = at', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Substitute v − u = at. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: triangle area. C1: substitution. A1: C (½t(v − u) with v − u = at).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg9df04319-t fg9df04319-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg9df04319-t">General derivation</title><desc id="fg9df04319-d">A straight v–t line from u at t = 0 to v at time t; the area is split into a rectangle of height u and a triangle of height v − u.</desc><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="335.3" y1="242" x2="335.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="335.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="179.6" x2="24" y2="179.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="179.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">u</text><line x1="20" y1="54.8" x2="24" y2="54.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="54.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v</text><polygon points="24,179.6 335.3,54.8 335.3,242 24,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="24,179.6 335.3,54.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="24,179.6 335.3,179.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><polyline points="335.3,242 335.3,54.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="179.7" y="214.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">ut</text><text x="241.9" y="142" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">½(v − u)t</text></svg>', 'A straight v–t line from u at t = 0 to v at time t; the area is split into a rectangle of height u and a triangle of height v − u.'),
('1867b74f-5d3d-577f-a391-3acc5f2781e8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 27, 27, 'For a car moving from 12 m s⁻¹ to 4.0 m s⁻¹ in 4.0 s, calculate the displacement using s = (u + v)t/2.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '32', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = (12 + 4.0) × 4.0 ÷ 2 = 32 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: equation. C1: value. A1: s = 32 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg7e72186c-t fg7e72186c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg7e72186c-t">Decelerating car</title><desc id="fg7e72186c-d">A straight v–t line falling from 12 to 4.0 m s⁻¹ over 4.0 s, with the trapezium under it shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="107.8" y1="34" x2="107.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="186.1" y1="34" x2="186.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="342.8" y1="34" x2="342.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="182.6" x2="382" y2="182.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="123.1" x2="382" y2="123.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="63.7" x2="382" y2="63.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="29.4,24 32.4,30.3 26.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="107.8" y1="242" x2="107.8" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="107.8" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="186.1" y1="242" x2="186.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="186.1" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="264.5" y1="242" x2="264.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="264.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="342.8" y1="242" x2="342.8" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="342.8" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="25.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="25.4" y1="182.6" x2="29.4" y2="182.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="182.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="25.4" y1="123.1" x2="29.4" y2="123.1" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="123.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="25.4" y1="63.7" x2="29.4" y2="63.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="63.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12</text><text x="205.7" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v / m s⁻¹</text><polygon points="29.4,63.7 342.8,182.6 342.8,242 29.4,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="29.4,63.7 342.8,182.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A straight v–t line falling from 12 to 4.0 m s⁻¹ over 4.0 s, with the trapezium under it shaded.'),
('01891868-2986-5958-80d5-1e63debbd333', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 28, 28, 'For the same car (12 → 4.0 m s⁻¹ in 4.0 s), calculate s using s = ut + ½at² to confirm the result.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '32', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (4.0 − 12) ÷ 4.0 = −2.0 m s⁻²; s = 12 × 4.0 + 0.5 × (−2.0) × 4.0² = 32 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a. C1: s. A1: s = 32 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a7f941ec-b06b-5c28-8a1b-8022579ae025', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 29, 29, 'A student says s = vt for an accelerating car. Why is this wrong?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It assumes the velocity is constant at its final value; with acceleration the average velocity is less than v', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Use the average velocity (u + v)/2. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: constant v assumed. C1: average velocity. A1: A (It assumes the velocity is constant at its final value; with acceleration the average velocity is less than v).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e0f70f69-47f9-5178-a0b5-f13bb645a512', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 30, 30, 'Show that the units of ut + ½at² are metres, and evaluate it for u = 0.50 m s⁻¹, a = 0.20 m s⁻², t = 10 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Units: (m s⁻¹)(s) = m and (m s⁻²)(s²) = m. s = 0.50 × 10 + 0.5 × 0.20 × 10² = 15 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: units. C1: value. A1: s = 15 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('b7ca96ac-9a0e-54e8-8c94-553151fb6261', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 31, 31, 'From v² = u² + 2as, derive an expression for s and calculate the stopping distance of a car from 26 m s⁻¹ with deceleration 6.5 m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '52', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = (v² − u²) ÷ 2a; with v = 0 and a = −6.5: s = 26² ÷ (2 × 6.5) = 52 m. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: rearrangement. C1: signs. C1: value. A1: s = 52 m.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('94d44681-c7cc-5ef6-86be-4dad93bf4ad2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 32, 32, 'Why does the derivation of s = ut + ½at² from a v–t graph require u, v and a to be in the same direction?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The graph and the areas assume one-dimensional motion with a chosen positive direction', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Signs handle opposite directions along one line. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: straight-line motion. C1: sign convention. A1: D (The graph and the areas assume one-dimensional motion with a chosen positive direction).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('00523e6c-3b05-51ec-b0ed-a52a0377fe62', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 33, 33, 'For u = 0, show that s = ½at² and v² = 2as are consistent by computing v from both for a = 4.0 m s⁻² and t = 2.5 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = 0.5 × 4.0 × 2.5² = 12.5 m; v = √(2 × 4.0 × 12.5) = 10 m s⁻¹, equal to at = 4.0 × 2.5 = 10 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: s. C1: v both ways. A1: v = 10 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('60c9d4a2-1468-5048-8a68-1807be76faf8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 34, 34, 'A ball is dropped. Using s = ½gt², calculate the ratio of distance fallen in the first 2.0 s to that in the first 1.0 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Ratio = (2.0 ÷ 1.0)² = 4.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: s ∝ t². C1: value. A1: ratio = 4.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6ccff714-5b9c-5a18-8981-444c239c7ca2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 35, 35, 'For uniform acceleration from rest, the distances in successive equal time intervals are in the ratio 1 : 3 : 5 : … Calculate the distance in the third second for a = 2.0 m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's(3) − s(2) = 0.5 × 2.0 × 3² − 0.5 × 2.0 × 2² = 5.0 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: s at 3 s and 2 s. C1: difference. A1: s = 5.0 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0ed11170-7a24-519e-848b-bd713308e86c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 36, 36, 'Which equation would you derive and use to find the time for a known u, v and s (a unknown)?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 's = (u + v)t/2, rearranged to t = 2s/(u + v)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'It is the only one without a. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: equation. C1: rearrangement. A1: B (s = (u + v)t/2, rearranged to t = 2s/(u + v)).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('7628727a-531a-552f-8ec9-a2efba3de3b7', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 37, 37, 'A sledge slows uniformly from 8.0 m s⁻¹ to 2.0 m s⁻¹ over 25 m. Calculate the time taken.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 2 × 25 ÷ (8.0 + 2.0) = 5.0 s. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: t = 2s/(u + v). C1: value. A1: t = 5.0 s.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a137b519-d728-5840-8f60-75a0a96b3aed', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 38, 38, 'Using the trapezium idea, find the displacement of a cyclist whose speed rises uniformly from 2.5 m s⁻¹ to 7.5 m s⁻¹ in 12 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '60', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = 0.5 × (2.5 + 7.5) × 12 = 60 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: trapezium. C1: value. A1: s = 60 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a92c1dd9-fe3f-5366-bdff-f99ffe3c1a5e', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 39, 39, 'Show that s = (u + v)t/2 and s = ut + ½at² agree for u = 3.0 m s⁻¹, a = 1.0 m s⁻², t = 6.0 s. Give s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '36', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 3.0 + 1.0 × 6.0 = 9.0 m s⁻¹; (3.0 + 9.0) × 6.0 ÷ 2 = 36 m and 3.0 × 6.0 + 0.5 × 1.0 × 6.0² = 36 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v. C1: both give 36 m. A1: s = 36 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1a972cb2-cba7-5956-9ea8-a234a5356e42', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 40, 40, 'A runner speeds up from 4.0 m s⁻¹ to 10 m s⁻¹ with a uniform acceleration of 3.0 m s⁻². Rearrange v² = u² + 2as to find the distance covered.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '14', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = (10² − 4.0²) ÷ (2 × 3.0) = 14 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: rearranged. C1: value. A1: s = 14 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgee5ef915-t fgee5ef915-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgee5ef915-t">Runner speeding up</title><desc id="fgee5ef915-d">A straight v–t line from 4.0 to 10 m s⁻¹ with gradient 3.0 m s⁻², with the area under it shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="34" x2="100" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="170.5" y1="34" x2="170.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="241" y1="34" x2="241" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="311.5" y1="34" x2="311.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="172.7" x2="382" y2="172.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="103.3" x2="382" y2="103.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="29.4,24 32.4,30.3 26.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="100" y1="242" x2="100" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="100" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.5</text><line x1="170.5" y1="242" x2="170.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><line x1="241" y1="242" x2="241" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="241" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5</text><line x1="311.5" y1="242" x2="311.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="311.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0</text><line x1="382" y1="242" x2="382" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="382" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.5</text><line x1="25.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="25.4" y1="172.7" x2="29.4" y2="172.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="172.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="25.4" y1="103.3" x2="29.4" y2="103.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="103.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="25.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12</text><text x="205.7" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v / m s⁻¹</text><polygon points="29.4,172.7 311.5,68.7 311.5,242 29.4,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="29.4,172.7 311.5,68.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A straight v–t line from 4.0 to 10 m s⁻¹ with gradient 3.0 m s⁻², with the area under it shaded.'),
('66451f65-97ca-5b71-a37e-71b9696ba447', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 41, 41, 'In deriving the equations of motion from a v–t graph, what is the gradient used for?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It defines the acceleration, giving a = (v − u)/t', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Gradient → v = u + at; area → s equations. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: gradient = a. C1: v = u + at. A1: D (It defines the acceleration, giving a = (v − u)/t).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5e87fc56-a2e7-54e5-972a-14c50b874e0d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 42, 42, 'Rearrange v² = u² + 2as to find u, and calculate u when v = 13 m s⁻¹, a = 2.0 m s⁻² and s = 36 m.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'u = √(v² − 2as) = √(13² − 2 × 2.0 × 36) = 5.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: rearranged. C1: value. A1: u = 5.0 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('cecb9d03-0004-5281-9433-f4ef87778352', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 43, 43, 'A v–t line rises from rest to 9.0 m s⁻¹ in 6.0 s. Using the triangle area, show that s = ½vt and calculate s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '27', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Area = ½ × base × height = 0.5 × 9.0 × 6.0 = 27 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: triangle. C1: value. A1: s = 27 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('bc7b038c-6a0a-5853-be17-b0c7e5152705', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 44, 44, 'Derive v² = u² + 2as from v = u + at and s = (u + v)t/2, then calculate v for u = 6.0 m s⁻¹, a = 1.5 m s⁻², s = 40 m.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12.49', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = (v − u)/a; s = (u + v)(v − u)/(2a) = (v² − u²)/(2a), so v² = u² + 2as. v = √(6.0² + 2 × 1.5 × 40) = 12.5 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: eliminate t. B1: difference of squares. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: v = 12.5 m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('689af20d-67b0-5833-aa49-22d3c14be960', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '69bb568e-7993-444e-9ce8-19ebbd98c526', 'a-level', '2.9', '9702 coursebook 2.9 · Deriving the equations of motion', 45, 45, 'An object accelerates uniformly from rest. (a) Use s = ½at² to show that the distance in the nth second is a(2n − 1)/2. (b) Calculate the distance in the 5th second for a = 3.0 m s⁻². (c) Calculate the total distance in the first 5 s.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '37.5', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) s(n) − s(n − 1) = ½a[n² − (n − 1)²] = a(2n − 1)/2. (b) 3.0 × (2 × 5 − 1) ÷ 2 = 13.5 m. (c) 0.5 × 3.0 × 5² = 37.5 m. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: difference of s. B1: algebra. C1: fifth second. M1: s = ½at². C1: value. A1: s = 37.5 m.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf2cfc24d-t fgf2cfc24d-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf2cfc24d-t">Distance in each second</title><desc id="fgf2cfc24d-d">A straight v–t line from rest with gradient 3.0 m s⁻² for 5.0 s; the strips for each second have areas in the ratio 1 : 3 : 5 : 7 : 9.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="100" y1="34" x2="100" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="170.5" y1="34" x2="170.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="241" y1="34" x2="241" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="311.5" y1="34" x2="311.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="203" x2="382" y2="203" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="164" x2="382" y2="164" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="125" x2="382" y2="125" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="86" x2="382" y2="86" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="47" x2="382" y2="47" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="29.4,24 32.4,30.3 26.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="100" y1="242" x2="100" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="100" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="centra