('f9bd5b47-e1fc-5d5c-a514-d83df1923243', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 14, 14, 'What can be found from a curved v–t graph by counting squares under it?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The displacement', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Area gives displacement for any v–t graph. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (The displacement).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('80f0fc4b-581f-5e86-aa12-4dbdc4052da6', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 15, 15, 'A tangent to a v–t curve rises 6.0 m s⁻¹ over 4.0 s. Calculate the acceleration it shows.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = 6.0 ÷ 4.0 = 1.5 m s⁻². Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: a = 1.5 m s⁻².', 1, NULL, NULL),
('a8beba11-ed65-5820-b7f1-a3cab2e49a7f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 16, 16, 'Why is the average acceleration over an interval not the same as the instantaneous acceleration for non-uniform motion?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The acceleration changes during the interval, so the average differs from the value at any one instant', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Only for uniform acceleration are they equal. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (The acceleration changes during the interval, so the average differs from the value at any one instant).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('0e9c3291-d830-5435-9ada-d87124529af2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 17, 17, 'A rocket''s speed rises from 100 m s⁻¹ to 250 m s⁻¹ in 5.0 s, with increasing acceleration. Calculate its average acceleration.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (250 − 100) ÷ 5.0 = 30 m s⁻². Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: Δv/t. A1: a = 30 m s⁻².', 2, NULL, NULL),
('1a99e66a-3da3-5a98-a3c8-46e742677785', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 18, 18, 'A car''s speed is 0, 4.0, 8.0 and 12 m s⁻¹ at t = 0, 1.0, 2.0 and 3.0 s. Calculate its acceleration.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Speed rises by 4.0 m s⁻¹ each second: a = 4.0 ÷ 1.0 = 4.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: constant increase. A1: a = 4.0 m s⁻².', 2, NULL, NULL),
('b402a84d-c6c3-5b2d-8270-84d631217b5d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 19, 19, 'Which of these has uniform acceleration?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A stone falling in a vacuum', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Only gravity acts on the stone. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (A stone falling in a vacuum).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('64dac64d-35ef-5d8d-9126-4fbd52d0fa28', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 20, 20, 'At t = 2.0 s a v–t curve has a tangent of gradient 5.0 m s⁻². Estimate the change in velocity in the next 0.10 s.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δv ≈ a Δt = 5.0 × 0.10 = 0.50 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: Δv = aΔt. A1: Δv = 0.50 m s⁻¹.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('0a1d4c65-595d-54c7-a286-3f47ddbe4ba2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 21, 21, 'A car''s speed increases by 2, then 4, then 6 m s⁻¹ in successive seconds. What kind of acceleration is this?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Increasing (non-uniform) acceleration', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The change per second is growing. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (Increasing (non-uniform) acceleration).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('5832aa80-359e-5834-b685-42225c5ad1fc', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 22, 22, 'Tangents to a v–t curve give accelerations of 8.0 m s⁻² at 1.0 s and 2.0 m s⁻² at 5.0 s. By how much has the acceleration fallen?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Fall = 8.0 − 2.0 = 6.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: difference. A1: Δa = 6.0 m s⁻².', 2, NULL, NULL),
('24b246ff-ebc2-5370-9ee6-56efe44cb5f8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 23, 23, 'Why does a rocket''s acceleration increase as it burns fuel, even with constant thrust?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Its mass decreases, so the same force gives a larger acceleration', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = F/m with m falling. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: mass decreases. C1: a = F/m. A1: B (Its mass decreases, so the same force gives a larger acceleration).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1e0ca29d-0b10-5428-9cd0-8e9da643cd4c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 24, 24, 'A car''s velocity is given by v = 0.30t² (v in m s⁻¹, t in s). Calculate its average acceleration between t = 2.0 s and t = 4.0 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.8', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v(2.0) = 1.2 m s⁻¹; v(4.0) = 4.8 m s⁻¹; a = (4.8 − 1.2) ÷ 2.0 = 1.8 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: both velocities. C1: Δv/Δt. A1: a = 1.8 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg37ed8436-t fg37ed8436-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg37ed8436-t">v = 0.30t²</title><desc id="fg37ed8436-d">The curve v = 0.30t² from 0 to 5.0 s, with the chord between t = 2.0 s and t = 4.0 s dashed.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="95.6" y1="34" x2="95.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="167.2" y1="34" x2="167.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.8" y1="34" x2="238.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310.4" y1="34" x2="310.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width