('da2aa899-38d3-5794-ba30-5643d067c776', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 25, 25, 'For v = 0.30t², is the acceleration uniform?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'No; the v–t graph is a curve, so the acceleration increases with time', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Here a = dv/dt = 0.60t, which grows with t. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: curved graph. C1: a increases. A1: C (No; the v–t graph is a curve, so the acceleration increases with time).', 3, NULL, NULL),
