('74c74077-47d3-59a1-9cb4-a1069fba5d91', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 27, 27, 'A sphere in oil has speeds 0.10, 0.17, 0.21, 0.23 m s⁻¹ at 0.1 s intervals. Calculate the average acceleration over the whole 0.3 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4333', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (0.23 − 0.10) ÷ 0.3 = 0.433 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: overall Δv. C1: ÷ 0.3 s. A1: a = 0.433 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a4fc22b8-2e6b-565a-9a72-61b24438680d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 28, 28, 'Why can s = ut + ½at² not be used to find how far a skydiver falls in the first 10 s?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Her acceleration is not constant because air resistance increases with speed', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'suvat needs uniform acceleration. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a not constant. C1: reason. A1: A (Her acceleration is not constant because air resistance increases with speed).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f68d6bbf-db68-5a55-97f4-ab4b9bb4195a', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 29, 29, 'An estimate of the area under a curved v–t graph gives 38 large squares, each 1.0 m s⁻¹ × 1.0 s. Estimate the displacement.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '38', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Each square = 1.0 × 1.0 = 1.0 m; s = 38 × 1.0 = 38 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: square value. C1: value. A1: s = 38 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('731c2743-904d-517d-aa39-196bd171366c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 30, 30, 'A car''s acceleration falls steadily from 4.0 m s⁻² at t = 0 to zero at t = 6.0 s. Using the area under its a–t graph, calculate its gain in speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δv = area under a–t graph = 0.5 × 4.0 × 6.0 = 12 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: area under a–t gives Δv. C1: triangle. A1: Δv = 12 m s⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg30e12051-t fg30e12051-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg30e12051-t">Acceleration–time graph</title><desc id="fg30e12051-d">An a–t graph falling in a straight line from 4.0 m s⁻² to zero at 6.0 s, with the triangle under it shaded.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="75.1" y1="34" x2="75.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="126.3" y1="34" x2="126.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="177.4" y1="34" x2="177.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="228.6" y1="34" x2="228.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="279.7" y1="34" x2="279.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.9" y1="34" x2="330.9" y2="242" style=