('f9e39d83-621c-5ba2-b138-b805213eb8c1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 33, 33, 'For that train (0.50 m s⁻² for 20 s, then 0.20 m s⁻² for 30 s from rest), calculate the total distance travelled.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '490', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Stage 1: 0.5 × 0.50 × 20² = 100 m, reaching 10 m s⁻¹. Stage 2: 10 × 30 + 0.5 × 0.20 × 30² = 390 m. Total = 100 + 390 = 490 m. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: stage 1. C1: stage 2. C1: total. A1: s = 490 m.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('0b2eb81f-405e-590b-88b7-05afab2e5acf', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 34, 34, 'A motion with two stages of different constant accelerations can be analysed with suvat. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The acceleration is uniform within each stage, so suvat applies to each stage separately', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Use the end of stage 1 as the start of stage 2. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: piecewise uniform. C1: link stages. A1: B (The acceleration is uniform within each stage, so suvat applies to each stage separately).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('61310282-b496-5d18-b9f2-623efccdb2d2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 35, 35, 'A ball falls with air resistance. Its speed is 8.6 m s⁻¹ after 1.0 s and 15.8 m s⁻¹ after 2.0 s. Calculate its average acceleration in the second second.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.2', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (15.8 − 8.6) ÷ 1.0 = 7.2 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δv. C1: ÷ 1.0 s. A1: a = 7.2 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2e63bfbe-7b29-52a2-a831-2c8009c4ae88', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 36, 36, 'In that fall (average acceleration 7.2 m s⁻² in the second second), why is it less than 9.81 m s⁻²?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Air resistance opposes the motion and grows with speed', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The resultant force is less than the weight. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: drag. C1: resultant force reduced. A1: C (Air resistance opposes the motion and grows with speed).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('df2ee80c-bc74-584a-a117-890e7de92966', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 37, 37, 'A sprinter''s speed is 0, 6.0, 8.5, 9.6 and 10.0 m s⁻¹ at t = 0, 1, 2, 3 and 4 s. Estimate the distance in the first 4 s by treating each second as uniform acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '29.1', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = (0 + 6.0)/2 + (6.0 + 8.5)/2 + (8.5 + 9.6)/2 + (9.6 + 10.0)/2 = 29.1 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: trapezia. C1: sum. A1: s = 29.1 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc373de88-t fgc373de88-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc373de88-t">Sprinter</title><desc id="fgc373de88-d">Speed readings 0, 6.0, 8.5, 9.6 and 10.0 m s⁻¹ at 0–4 s joined by straight lines, with the area (trapezia) shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="117.6" y1="34" x2="117.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="293.9" y1="34" x2="293.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="172.7" x2="382" y2="172