('e35fb20c-6632-5c4d-be97-31d14dd917bc', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '643b6cd1-3fbe-4618-9330-b9d737f06161', 'a-level', '2.10', '9702 coursebook 2.10 · Uniform and non-uniform acceleration', 54, 54, 'A car starting from rest has acceleration 3.0 m s⁻² for the first 4.0 s, after which its acceleration decreases uniformly to zero at 10 s. (a) Calculate its speed at 4.0 s. (b) Calculate its speed at 10 s from the area under the a–t graph.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '21', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 3.0 × 4.0 = 12 m s⁻¹. (b) v = 12 + 0.5 × 3.0 × 6.0 = 21 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: rectangle. M1: triangle area. C1: sum. C1: value. A1: v = 21 m s⁻¹.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf717fe7e-t fgf717fe7e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf717fe7e-t">a–t graph</title><desc id="fgf717fe7e-d">An a–t graph constant at 3.0 m s⁻² for 4.0 s and then falling in a straight line to zero at 10 s, with the area shaded.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="89.1" y1="34" x2="89.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154.2" y1="34" x2="154.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="219.3" y1="34" x2="219.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284.4" y1="34" x2="284.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.5" y1="34" x2="349.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width